agentic-trader
==============

This project is adapted from FriesTrader:

    https://github.com/YizhiSong/FriesTrader
    Copyright (c) 2026 Yizhi Song
    MIT License

The two-phase pipeline design (Phase A screening/thesis, Phase B
re-verification and mechanical risk enforcement), the risk-rule model,
the deterministic risk-math scripts, and the Phase A/Phase B task specs
all originate there. The MIT license text those were released under is
reproduced in LICENSE and continues to cover that work.

Changes made in this repository:

- Added a pytest suite covering all five risk scripts through their real
  CLI contract, plus CI running it on every push.
- Take-profit tiers now carry stable `id`s, and "already fired this
  holding period" is keyed on those ids rather than on each tier's
  `gain_pct`. Previously, retuning a tier's threshold mid-holding-period
  made an already-fired tier look unfired and re-sold against the same
  position.
- The conviction sizing table moved out of a prompt string in
  PHASE_B_TASK.md and into `risk_rules.json`, so every risk limit lives
  in one auditable file. `position_sizing.py` now rejects a config whose
  tiers exceed `max_position_pct_of_account`, making that cap a real
  backstop rather than a per-candidate check that could never fire.
- All five scripts share one failure contract (`scripts/_common.py`):
  one JSON object on stdout and exit 0 on success, one JSON `{"error":
  ...}` on stderr and exit 1 on failure, never a traceback. Input
  validation was extended accordingly.
